| `install_sources.python_index` | string or null | `null` | null, or an https URL with a host, a valid port if any, and no `@`, `?`, `#`, backslash, whitespace or control character | `scripts/install_sources.py` and `scripts/check_venv.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `install_sources.python_index` row | Set, every CI adapter's `pip install` step passes it as `--index-url`, and the fix command `make check-venv` prints carries `--index-url <url>`; null passes nothing, so pip's own configuration (`pip.conf`, `PIP_INDEX_URL`) holds. A refused value is exit 14, never showing a value that holds an `@`. Absent, the reader writes `[using default] install_sources.python_index = null` to stderr. | the secret scanner's download: `secrets.scanner.release_url` | always |
